  "input": "2015 Year-End PBC List.pdf",
  "source": "https://bpb-us-e2.wpmucdn.com/sites.uclawsf.edu/dist/6/18/files/2016/01/3-_RFP_56-0170_APP_III_2015-YEAR-END-PBC-List-20uz1ia.pdf",
  "about": "The external auditor's year-end PBC list for UC Hastings College of the Law (now UC Law SF), fiscal year ended June 30, 2015, published unchanged as Appendix III of the college's audit RFP 56-0170. A text PDF of a table: Audit Type, Category, Item ID (FSC-01, FSC-01a, FSF-01, SA-01), a section-local number and the request, with cells wrapped over several lines. Three parts: college, foundation and single audit (A-133). FSC-01i and FSC-02g are notes, not requests, and are left out. Ramp-answerable: FSC-38 (check register 7/1/15 to 9/8/15 with support for disbursements over $50,000), FSC-71 and FSF-17 (legal expense GL detail with supporting invoices over $5,000 and $1,000); the GL-detail half of those is outside Ramp. Judgment calls: FSC-08 says 'year ended 6/30/14' but asks for FY15 transactions in the next sentence, scored as FY15. FSF-06 says 'entire 2014 fiscal year', likely a stale carry-over, scored as written (FY14). FSC-18's 'five business days' either side of year end is scored 2015-06-23 to 2015-07-08 (July 3, 2015 was a bank holiday). SA-11 'in CY?' names no year, scored as FY15. FSF-07 (minutes 'for fiscal year 2015 and up to date') runs to the fieldwork date, so it has no end date. FSC-10 asks for expense GL detail and says selections will follow; it stays unsupported until they do. Point-in-time items ('as of 6/30/15') use the fiscal year, as elsewhere in the corpus. Thresholds on variance requests (fluxes over $100,000 and 10%) are recorded as the dollar amount.",
